    "atom::349f23b247bb74e7f21b4e09": {
      "atom_id": "atom::349f23b247bb74e7f21b4e09",
      "source_handle": "P0363",
      "field_path": [
        "local_passages"
      ],
      "value": {
        "external_calls": 0,
        "passages": [
          {
            "best_sentence": "Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics.",
            "card_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\paper_cards\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\reading\\cards\\9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\\0e352726189f698ed7200afeb2df9e1f\\attempt-01\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json",
            "doi": "10.25259/ijmio_8_2026",
            "limits": [],
            "match_terms": [
              "粪菌移植",
              "gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours",
              "ici",
              "nsclc",
              "rcc"
            ],
            "material_depth": "fulltext",
            "paper_id": "9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1",
            "pool_action": "already_in_pool",
            "reading_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\paper_cards\\20260922_microbiome_batch\\materials\\9db1c1ced73dca207c6289b20b4a2914a09ca2b1\\snapshot-a22ccfd4fa2ec07e546e769c",
            "score": 45.119645,
            "section_path": [],
            "segment_kind": "document_block",
            "source_handle": "P0363",
            "text": "Practical clinical considerations for microbiome-related interventions in patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics. Artificial intelligence (AI)-assisted language tools were used during manuscript drafting and language refinement.All scientific content, interpretation, refere",
            "title": "The gut microbiome–tumor microenvironment axis in immunotherapy response: Mechanistic insights and clinical implications",
            "usable_fields": [],
            "year": "2026"
          }
        ],
        "question": "How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。",
        "reading_mode": "focused_local_search"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
