    "atom::af989328995494c8922ca744": {
      "atom_id": "atom::af989328995494c8922ca744",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "work_summary"
      ],
      "value": "本研究是一项前瞻性观察研究，旨在探讨肠道微生物组与胃肠道癌症患者接受免疫治疗引发的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）之间的关联。研究纳入了95名完成基线粪便采样且仅接受单一或联合PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂治疗的患者，通过宏基因组测序分析其基线微生物组成及代谢通路。结果显示，整体微生物多样性在有无irAEs患者间无显著差异，但特定菌种和代谢通路存在差异：Ruminococcus callidus和Bacteroides xylanisolvens在无严重irAEs患者中富集，而某些致病菌或条件致病菌在irAEs患者中升高。此外，尿素循环及相关氨基酸合成通路与irAEs发生有关，且不同癌症类型和特定器官毒性（如皮肤、血液、内分泌、肝脏）表现出不同的微生物特征。该研究为理解irAEs的微生物机制提供了基础数据，但缺乏外部验证队列和实验验证。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::f0cc6e0c83ee784bd4a38db82bde4756d2ac7671c3ec66bd91ff60ad677832a9",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::81c5e7a7665d3a97efbcc82b": {
      "atom_id": "atom::81c5e7a7665d3a97efbcc82b",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "该论文为综述提供了胃肠道癌症特定背景下，肠道微生物组与免疫治疗不良反应（irAEs）关联的详细实证数据。不同于以往主要集中在黑色素瘤或肺癌的研究，本文聚焦于消化道肿瘤，指出了在此类人群中特定的保护性或风险性微生物标志物（如R. callidus）及代谢通路（尿素循环），并强调了irAEs的器官特异性和癌症类型依赖性。这些发现可用于构建关于“不同实体瘤类型中微生物对免疫治疗副作用的影响”以及“微生物代谢功能介导irAEs的潜在机制”的论述素材。",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::175759667964ff4498bf8966286caf8f0fe7f2c98c29c6e2689617e6aade4c93",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::e386fd22d8c544b9c1efcca4": {
      "atom_id": "atom::e386fd22d8c544b9c1efcca4",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "仅限于相关性，不能证明因果。样本来自单一中心，可能存在选择偏倚。未涵盖所有类型的固体瘤。",
        "contribution": "提供了胃肠道癌症患者中，基线微生物组成与irAEs发生风险的关联证据。具体指出Ruminococcus callidus和Bacteroides xylanisolvens的富集与较低的重症irAEs风险相关，而某些细菌（如B. dentium, R. mucilaginosa）的升高与irAEs发生相关。",
        "facet_id": "F1"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::7ddea1d8a59caab78f3f4350e76ea3ecee88b2645f4953a08d2d07d20db7a33d",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::4a1e19ca983f75abd0f28704": {
      "atom_id": "atom::4a1e19ca983f75abd0f28704",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "用于支持综述中关于“特定肠道菌群特征可预测免疫治疗不良反应风险”的观点，特别是针对消化道肿瘤这一亚群。可与黑色素瘤或其他癌种的发现进行对比，展示菌群-irAEs关联的肿瘤类型特异性。",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::6ae3f3135cd6c234208e6733b863fe34f50b336707d87eeb4c39df928b787506",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::4f793f32a90597b4a0d249f5": {
      "atom_id": "atom::4f793f32a90597b4a0d249f5",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "代谢通路的富集是观察性结果，作者承认缺乏实验验证来确认这些通路直接导致或保护免受irAEs。引用的机制多来自其他疾病模型或癌种，需注明外推的不确定性。",
        "contribution": "提出了微生物代谢功能可能介导irAEs的线索。发现尿素循环（urea cycle）及瓜氨酸/精氨酸生物合成通路在无irAEs或低毒性患者中富集。讨论了精氨酸代谢在免疫调节中的潜在作用，并引用了其他研究中益生菌（如乳酸杆菌、双歧杆菌）通过调节Treg细胞或IL-10缓解炎症的机制。",
        "facet_id": "F2"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::7ddea1d8a59caab78f3f4350e76ea3ecee88b2645f4953a08d2d07d20db7a33d",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::ff5f1c87738ed2caac1cc62e": {
      "atom_id": "atom::ff5f1c87738ed2caac1cc62e",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "用于综述中探讨“微生物代谢产物如何影响宿主免疫反应从而导致irAEs”的机制部分。特别是尿素循环和氨基酸代谢作为潜在的共同机制路径。也可用于讨论益生菌补充剂作为预防irAEs策略的理论基础。",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::6ae3f3135cd6c234208e6733b863fe34f50b336707d87eeb4c39df928b787506",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::5aee41876112ff2a057ab15f": {
      "atom_id": "atom::5aee41876112ff2a057ab15f",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "broader_review_uses"
      ],
      "value": {
        "material": "研究发现不同癌症类型（食管、胃、结肠）的irAEs具有截然不同的微生物特征。例如，胃癌中益生菌（乳酸杆菌、双歧杆菌）富集与低毒性相关，而结肠癌中Bacteroides stercoris与高毒性相关。"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::3880c225b737e554fa79475566f8768104185327494e05e81f379ae67b3a463a",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::81d761c3553cdd5bda53d640": {
      "atom_id": "atom::81d761c3553cdd5bda53d640",
      "source_handle": "P0011",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "broader_review_uses",
        "connection_to_review"
      ],
      "value": "支持综述中关于“情境依赖性（Context-dependency）”的论点，即微生物对免疫治疗疗效或毒性的影响高度依赖于肿瘤类型和局部解剖环境。",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::9434601012338f320affc14b004fedd527e07481e307d66fd6a26b18e6d628cf",
          "field_path": [
